WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.520
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.850
Hi, I am Pamela Pairo,
PhD, Biological Sciences

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.870
from Argentina.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.690
In this presentation, I'm
going to show you how to create

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.620
A multilingual website
using blogdown, Hugo, and Netlify.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.890
First of all, why do you
need a personal website?

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.190
Having apersonal website is
another way to showcase your CV

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:27.270
or resume with a style and gives
you the freedom to be creative.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.720
By writing posts, you will
practice your communication

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.600
skills, you can exchange
knowledge with colleagues,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.360
and therefore, your
network will be expanded.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.240
In my experience, when I
came across with difficulties

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.080
or doubts, I had able to solve
the issue, thanks to the posts

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.770
shared by others.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.010
And finally, the
personal website

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.630
is a platform to
connect with a world.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:53.040
For those of us who aren't
native English speakers,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.500
it's fundamental to cover
multilingual websites.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.610
In English, to disseminate our
work to the global community,

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.460
and in our native language,
to make our website

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:06.190
content more inclusive and
accessible for everyone.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:07.770
Let's get started.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.850
We began creating a new
report in our GitHub account.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:16.410
Then in RStudio, create a
new project with contribution

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.750
and then load blogdown and Hugo.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.510
You can look at all the
themes and select one

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.280
on each Hugo website.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.490
After that, you will
have the default version

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.230
of the site in the viewer panel
so it's time to customize.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:35.010
The main files that are part of
the website are showing here.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.110
In config.toml is
where it is located

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.730
global settings for the site.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:44.100
And in the config/default
folder are the params.toml,

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.620
where you can change
the color theme,

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:51.510
the font size of your website,
and add your contact details.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.320
To change what appears in
the navigation menu bar

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.690
is necessary to edit
the menus.toml file.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:01.230
And in language.toml is where
you can change the language

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.220
setting.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:06.480
And how to make your personal
website multilingual?

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.720
I'm going to show you an example
of the bilingual website,

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.880
English and Spanish.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.140
In the language.toml,
you have to uncomment

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.690
the lines for
a second language

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.330
to configure your website.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.150
Here, we have the information
about the English part,

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.930
for example, the language
code, where it's located

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.760
the content, and the title.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.660
Note that the abbreviation of
the languages are predefined.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:37.050
And so if you want a Portuguese
website, for example,

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:41.100
you need to check which is
the correct abbreviation.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:46.140
Then each language will need
their own menus.toml file

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:51.300
and a subfolder within
the content folder.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.570
Finally, choose the
default language

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.170
that the visitors will see
when they visit your page.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:01.800
And for make it visible that
the website is multilingual,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.660
check in params.toml that
show language is true.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.760
When you're done with
your edits and you

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.080
are happy with your website,
it's time to put it online.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.320
One way to do this
is using netlify.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.150
One of the advantages of
deploying your website

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.210
through netlify is that
it allows you

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.840
to have a static site
for free and easily.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.350
Basically, it connects to the
remote repository on GitHub

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.370
to deploy.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:32.220
Every change that it
makes on the website

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:38.440
it will be automatically updated
up there to push to GitHub.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.910
It's important that the
Hugo version that you're

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:47.930
running locally must match
with the version that

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.040
Netlify is going to
use to build your site.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.670
And how to do that?

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:56.950
Check first your
local version of Hugo

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:02.020
and pick up that netlify.toml
to your project root directory

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.720
and specify the Hugo version.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:12.520
Then go to the Netlify web
page and login with GitHub

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.630
to select the report you've
been working with blogdown.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:20.570
You will see something like
this but with your information.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:25.370
Go to show advanced and just
in case, write a Hugo version,

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.300
and finally, you will
have your website.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.940
In the latest
version of blogdown,

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:35.710
you can set up the Hugo
version by writing this code

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:41.850
and tell to Netlify the Hugo
version with this function.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.880
If you want more
information, here

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.880
are some blogs that I used
in this presentation

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:52.510
and you can find me on my
website and on Twitter.

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:54.350
Thank you.

